From c6f950f852d43433eb8b905795765c60d8f27110 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Alessandro Fontana <alessandro.fontana@pm.me>
Date: Fri, 14 Aug 2026 21:30:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] extcon: sm5502: set the detection timing at probe

TIMING_SET1 is left at its reset value, which selects a 50 ms detection
window.  The vendor driver programs 200 ms instead, and that difference
shows when a cable is already plugged in as the system boots: the chip
finishes its measurement before the host has answered and settles on a
plain SDP port.

On a Galaxy Tab A (SM-T580) booting with the cable in a charging
downstream port leaves DEV_TYPE1 at 0x04 for good - the chip does not
repeat the measurement on its own, so the extcon device reports SDP and
the charger stays at the 500 mA limit until the cable is cycled by hand.
Writing 200 ms at probe, as the vendor driver does, gives the
measurement enough room to land on the right answer.

The key press timing is programmed alongside it, matching the vendor
value, so that the whole register is defined rather than half of it
inheriting the reset default.

Note that reg_data entries with invert unset are written complemented,
so this entry carries invert set in order to reach the register as it
is.
---
 drivers/extcon/extcon-sm5502.c | 7 +++++++
 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/extcon/extcon-sm5502.c b/drivers/extcon/extcon-sm5502.c
index 7933db77c1..c2a0d94dbc 100644
--- a/drivers/extcon/extcon-sm5502.c
+++ b/drivers/extcon/extcon-sm5502.c
@@ -81,6 +81,13 @@ static struct reg_data sm5502_reg_data[] = {
 		.reg = SM5502_REG_CONTROL,
 		.val = SM5502_REG_CONTROL_MASK_INT_MASK,
 		.invert = false,
+	}, {
+		.reg = SM5502_REG_TIMING_SET1,
+		.val = (TIMING_ADC_DET_200MS
+				<< SM5502_REG_TIMING_SET1_ADC_DET_SHIFT)
+			| (TIMING_KEY_PRESS_100MS
+				<< SM5502_REG_TIMING_SET1_KEY_PRESS_SHIFT),
+		.invert = true,
 	}, {
 		.reg = SM5502_REG_INTMASK1,
 		.val = SM5502_REG_INTM1_KP_MASK
-- 
2.47.3

